# The Caddy front (atlas-tls) on Red Hat's Universal Base Image, for OpenShift (TASK-1478, ARO 1.3).
#
# WHY. docs/oss/research/openshift-aro.md, questions 1 and 3: on ARO Caddy stays, as the
# `atlas-tls` Deployment behind a re-encrypt Route, and the platform wants a UBI image. There is
# no official UBI Caddy image, so this builds one. Opt-in: only images.yml builds it, and
# deploy/caddy/Dockerfile (the compose install's atlas-tls and the homelab's front) is unchanged.
#
# WHAT IS IN IT. Stock Caddy and no plugin. The one plugin of deploy/caddy/Dockerfile,
# caddy-dns/cloudflare, exists for ACME DNS-01, and on OpenShift there is no ACME: the public
# certificate is the router's, and every certificate inside the namespace comes from the
# OpenShift service CA (research doc, question 3). Leaving it out also leaves its dependency
# graph out of the scanned binary.
#
# BUILD. xcaddy on ubi9/go-toolset (Go 1.26, which Caddy 2.11 needs), CGO off, so the binary is
# static and runs on ubi9/ubi-micro (no package manager, no CA bundle: every upstream Caddy
# dials is verified against a mounted CA file, and the OpenShift Caddyfile must keep ACME off,
# `auto_https disable_certs` or `off`, or Caddy tries to order a certificate for the public host).
# Caddy and xcaddy are pinned to exact release tags below and Go verifies every module against
# the checksum database, so the binary is reproducible from this file. Caddy v2.11.9 requires
# go-jose v4.1.6 itself, so deploy/caddy/Dockerfile's go-jose `--replace` (TASK-1434) has nothing
# to do here. It requires x/net v0.60.0, though: x/net is forced to v0.62.0 below (2026-11-10,
# CVE-2026-78661, HIGH, x/net/html DoS, fixed in 0.62.0). `--replace` writes a go.mod replace
# directive to an exact tag, so only that one module moves. Drop it once CADDY_VERSION requires
# x/net >= 0.62.0.
# To bump Caddy, change CADDY_VERSION; the base images are tag@digest (tools/ci/check_pins.py)
# and Dependabot's docker ecosystem watches /deploy/caddy.
#
# RUNTIME. Any UID in group 0 (OpenShift's restricted SCC), numeric USER, no low port: the
# OpenShift Caddyfile listens on 8443 and 9443. Caddy writes its state under XDG_DATA_HOME and
# its autosaved config under XDG_CONFIG_HOME: both exist in the image, group 0 and
# group-writable, and the ARO manifests mount an emptyDir on each so the root filesystem can be
# read-only. HOME=/tmp for anything else that looks for one. No HEALTHCHECK: Kubernetes probes
# the pod, and Docker's HEALTHCHECK is not used there.
FROM registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9/go-toolset:1.26@sha256:0e3894cea4fc077084245e8aa2befc8a7d91a4f60fbf850f0b5b555cbe62ee26 AS builder
ARG CADDY_VERSION=v2.11.9
ARG XCADDY_VERSION=v0.4.7
ENV CGO_ENABLED=0
RUN go install "github.com/caddyserver/xcaddy/cmd/xcaddy@${XCADDY_VERSION}" \
 && "$(go env GOPATH)/bin/xcaddy" build "${CADDY_VERSION}" --output /tmp/caddy \
      --replace golang.org/x/net=golang.org/x/net@v0.62.0 \
 && /tmp/caddy version
# Caddy's own licence (Apache-2.0), from the module the binary was built from, for /licenses.
RUN cp "$(go env GOMODCACHE)/github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2@${CADDY_VERSION}/LICENSE" /tmp/caddy-LICENSE

FROM registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9/ubi-micro:9.8@sha256:d3499a0896e2d6a1642f922615831bc5c2fd513bbb34f3446cabba530d9d54a2
COPY --from=builder /tmp/caddy /usr/bin/caddy
RUN mkdir -p /config /data /etc/caddy \
 && chgrp 0 /config /data \
 && chmod 0775 /config /data
# /licenses and the certification labels (TASK-1483; `preflight check container`): this
# repository's LICENSE and NOTICE (the build recipe and configuration) and Caddy's licence. The
# repository root is outside this build context (deploy/caddy/), so the build is handed it as the
# NAMED BUILD CONTEXT `repo` (`--build-context repo=.` from the root; images.yml's
# `build-contexts:`); the comment below declares it to tools/ci/check_pins.py. The ARGs come
# after the last RUN, so a new version re-labels the image without rebuilding a layer.
# build-context: repo
COPY --from=repo LICENSE NOTICE /licenses/
COPY --from=builder /tmp/caddy-LICENSE /licenses/caddy/LICENSE
ENV XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/config \
    XDG_DATA_HOME=/data \
    HOME=/tmp
USER 10001:0
EXPOSE 8443 9443
CMD ["caddy", "run", "--config", "/etc/caddy/Caddyfile", "--adapter", "caddyfile"]
ARG ATLAS_VERSION=dev
ARG ATLAS_RELEASE=dev
LABEL name="gradinai-atlas-tls-ubi" \
      vendor="gradinai-atlas" \
      maintainer="gradinai-atlas" \
      version="${ATLAS_VERSION}" \
      release="${ATLAS_RELEASE}" \
      summary="Atlas TLS front (atlas-tls, Caddy) on Red Hat UBI 9" \
      description="Stock Caddy, no plugin and no ACME, terminating the re-encrypt Route and the service-CA legs to atlas-api and atlas-mcp, non-root under any UID in group 0, for OpenShift." \
      io.k8s.display-name="Atlas TLS front (atlas-tls)" \
      io.k8s.description="Stock Caddy, no plugin and no ACME, terminating the re-encrypt Route and the service-CA legs to atlas-api and atlas-mcp, non-root under any UID in group 0, for OpenShift." \
      org.opencontainers.image.licenses="Apache-2.0"
